      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nenum verity_block_type;\n\nDECLARE_HOOK(android_vh_handle_error,\n\t\tTP_PROTO(struct dm_verity *v, enum verity_block_type type,\n\t\t\tunsigned long long block, struct dm_verity_io *io,\n\t\t\tconst u8 *data, const u8 *want_digest),\n\t\tTP_ARGS(v, type, block, io, data, want_digest));\n```\n\nIf I change it to \u0027enum\u0027 like above, I will encounter an error relate to variable has incomplete type like the below:\nXXXXXX/android16/out/bazel/output_user_root/9d0efe60da054428701ed198db7be3fe/sandbox/linux-sandbox/8/execroot/_main/common/include/trace/hooks/dmv_debug.h:21:56: error: variable has incomplete type \u0027enum verity_block_type\u0027\n   21 |                 TP_PROTO(struct dm_verity *v, enum verity_block_type type,\n\nTo fix it, I need to include header dm-verity.h like that: \n```#include \"../../../drivers/md/dm-verity.h\"```\nBut as I know, we should not include header file in the hooks file. That why I change \u0027enum\u0027 to \u0027int\u0027 type.",
